T:Os Daw fy Nghariad i Yma Heno (version 2)
T:Os Daw fy Nghariad Yma Heno
T:If My Love Comes Here Tonight
R:cân
S:https://amgueddfa.cymru/casgliadau/caneuongwerin/?id=27 (collected by D. Roy Saer)
N:Sung by Thomas Williams (born 1899), a postman, of 2 Salem Terrace, Sarn Mellteyrn, near Aberdaron, Caernarfonshire; recorded 9.10.64 (St Fagans tape 817). The song was very popular among the farm servants of Llŷn when he learnt it, in the years before the First World War.
N:The second part is sung three times, for verses 2, 3 and 4 (D.S. twice on the score). In bar 3 the singer sang D for the last F ("a" of "ym-a") in one of his four recordings. In bar 10 the score also gives the crotchet E ("ddo") as two small notes, a dotted quaver and a semiquaver E, for a verse with an extra syllable.
%%version Thomas Williams
